  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat, 2026-11-16. The maintainer set the priority `P2` in his own words:\n\n> \"Issue; p2; Log framerate to debug info as a value when it changes in performance once - and if it keeps jumping around log just every 10s or something like that.. Make debug info \"dockable\" as well.\"\n\nWanted, part 1 - frame rate in the debug info:\n\n- The debug info shows the frame rate (and the frame time in ms) as a value.\n- When the frame rate changes to a different level, the debug info logs one line with the new value. Use a threshold, so that small noise logs nothing.\n- When the frame rate does not become stable, the debug info logs at most one line each 10 s. That line gives the minimum, the maximum and the mean of the interval.\n- An idle application that does not repaint logs nothing.\n\nWanted, part 2 - dockable debug info:\n\n- The user can dock the debug info panel as the other panels dock, and can undock it again.\n- The dock position is part of the saved layout.\n\nRules:\n\n- The measurement costs no work in proportion to the model. It reads the frame times that the application has (frame cost rule, #2238). The log does not request a repaint.\n- The log rate limit applies to the `gpu: slow frame` lines too, or the issue says why not.\n- Panel layout is ephemeral UI state, not a command.\n- The text is plain English.\n\nDone means: a unit test pins the log rule (one line for one level change; no more than one line each 10 s when the value moves; no line when idle); a structural test pins that the debug info panel is present docked and undocked; the PR has before and after screenshots.\n",
